  "summary": "V444-V447 HELD T040/M018 shared nominal byte-image prerequisite for union storage. Existing plain byte classification, encoder and decoder now support actual prepared nominal structs through DeclarationFacts/LayoutTable instances and the one repr-aware layout algorithm. Reconstruction uses ordinary construction guards/tickets and grants no Copy or source authority. Transmute consumes its actual source ticket/owned field graph without guest Drop instead of orphaning it in moved_in; nominal zeroed/transmute destinations retain their own ordinary Drop. Image windows validate conversions/addition/ranges before access, including ZST windows, rather than fabricating zeros/ignoring writes. V444 unchanged transmute-const.rs fails19dispatches/3calls/1initializer; final V447 completes58dispatches/3calls/1initializer, unit/empty streams/cleanup in owning2015. V445 all16edition/origin const-image worlds and source-no-Drop/destination-once controls pass; its3/4control batch retains the combined formatter-signature failure. Controlled V446 production baseline654e0c7 reproduces that exact formatter failure with the same unchanged test and helper; it stays failed/inherited, not waived. Final V447 both builds and3/3scoped boundary/ownership/size controls pass; nominal zeroed is exercised in all4editions. Additional unchanged transmute-array-to-scalar still fails6dispatches at explicit Type source-signature admission. One newly passing distinct upstream runtime case against measured pre-change654e0c7, not a suite sweep or task/milestone/architecture closure. Union canonical backing/view coherence, projections/references/moves/Copy/cleanup, enum/provenance images, complete source signatures and full upstream solver/common-engine joins remain held. JIT stays gated.",
